{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["<b>קרבת</b> — I drew near to one of the angels standing there to serve the Ancient of Days, and all this was in a dream." "<b>ויציבא אבעא</b> — And the matter was firm: I asked of him." "<b>על דנא</b> — Concerning this, that he would explain to me this dream. And he said: these four beasts are four kingdoms, and he said 'kings' because the son is reckoned like the father, as in the kingdom of Chaldea. And the meaning of 'but the holy ones of the Most High' — at the end of the kingdom the holy ones of the Most High will receive the kingdom forever and ever. And he returned to mention the matters of the fourth beast, and mentioned now what he did not mention at first: that the little horn will wage war against Israel and prevail against them. And the angel explained to him that this last king of the kingdom of Ishmael will do great evil to Israel, and this is 'and he shall wear out the holy ones of the Most High.' And 'he shall think to change the times of Israel and their law,' and Israel shall be in distress, 'until a time and times and half a time' — and this I shall explain in the verse 'until a time, times, and half.' And verified is what I said, that the angel said: 'and the kingdom shall be given to the people of the holy ones of the Most High.'"], :book :daniel, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 7, :notes {2 "Ibn Ezra here quotes and interprets a sequence of Aramaic phrases from Daniel 7, weaving them together; I have retained the Aramaic script where he quotes it directly."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Daniel - Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/daniel"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:20:26.412511939Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}